+# Feature Specification: Bulk import
+
+- **FR-001**: `importTasks(list, text)` is exported from `src/index.ts`. `text` holds one task per line, as `title;priority;tags`.
+- **FR-002**: The priority may be empty (a normal task); the tags are separated by spaces and may be empty. A line with only a title is valid.
+- **FR-003**: Blank lines (empty or only spaces) are skipped. Lines end with `\n` or `\r\n`.
+- **FR-004**: Every valid line is added to the list through `list.add`, so the usual rules apply (title, priority, tags, duplicate title).
+- **FR-005**: It returns `{ imported, rejected }`: `imported` counts the added tasks; `rejected` lists each line not added as `{ line, reason }`, `line` counting from 1 over all lines, blank ones included. `reason` is the message of the error.
+- **FR-006**: A line with more than three `;`-separated fields is rejected. A rejected line does not stop the others, and never throws.
